{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"ravenous-centric-guppy","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Problem\n\nFix-version sync (ADR 0124, epic `inferior-seaborgium-aruanas`) is tested only against fakes. Unit tests cover the diffs, the transport writes and the release alerts. The one integration test, `tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_releases_roundtrip.py`, runs real `reconcile_once` passes over an in-memory Jira fake. Production was checked live once, against Jira Cloud (`plucky-jetblack-parrot`, `cognitive-sooty-angelfish`).\n\nThe Jira DC suite in `tests/external/live_jira_dc` has no fix-version test. That suite runs a real Jira DC server in Docker, in the `jira-dc-harness` job of `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml`. The DC write path (`src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py`) and the DC version read have never run against a real server.\n\n## Plan\n\nAdd a fix-version scenario module to `tests/external/live_jira_dc`. Reuse that suite's existing fixtures: the harness project, the bridge configuration and the reconcile runner. Follow the patterns in `test_multi_project_rehearsal.py` and `test_transport.py`. The scenario runs real reconcile passes against the Docker DC server and covers:\n\n1. Inbound sync: a version created in the DC project through the REST API and set on an issue's `fixVersions` appears in the bound rebar ticket's `releases`.\n2. Outbound add: a release added in rebar for a version the project has is written to the issue's `fixVersions`. Adding a second release also writes it and keeps the first, so the write is per item.\n3. Outbound remove: a release removed in rebar disappears from `fixVersions`, and the other entries stay.\n4. A missing version is held back: a release naming a version the DC project lacks is not written. Instead the ticket gets a BRIDGE_ALERT, and the alert clears once that version is created and a later pass writes it.\n\nThe test must leave the harness project clean, with no leftover versions or issues that would affect other tests in the module order.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A new test module under `tests/external/live_jira_dc/` covers scenarios 1 to 4 above against the Docker DC server, with real reconcile passes and no fakes on the Jira side.\n- [ ] Every new test carries the `external` marker. The new tests are picked up by `pytest -m external tests/external/live_jira_dc`, the command the `jira-dc-harness` job runs.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A `jira-dc-harness` run of `external-integration.yml` on a commit containing the new module passes, with the new tests listed as passed. The run URL is recorded in a comment on this ticket.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes on the change.\n- [ ] `tests/external/live_jira_dc/README.md` lists the new scenario.\n","id":"af08-19c2-87b4-41d3","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Live-test fix-version sync in the Jira DC Docker suite"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794513974422110663,"uuid":"37735220-f256-41ca-9669-afdeb6be1df8"}